  "clues": {
    "kinetics": "A high-fat meal barely changes total exposure, with AUC up about 8%. About 82% is protein bound, and the drug is metabolized by CYP3A.",
    "substance": "A crystalline, non-chiral solid with a molecular weight of 434.5 and low solubility across the physiological pH range.",
    "product": "Approved under an NDA as 100 mg and 150 mg tablets, dosed twice daily.",
    "safety": "No boxed warning. Nausea and fatigue are the most common adverse reactions.",
    "indication": "Maintenance treatment of advanced ovarian, fallopian tube or peritoneal cancer after platinum chemotherapy, including with bevacizumab in biomarker-selected disease.",
    "mechanism": "Inhibits PARP enzymes, trapping them on DNA; cytotoxicity is greatest where BRCA1/2 or homologous recombination repair is deficient."
  },
  "tell": "Itraconazole, a strong CYP3A inhibitor, raises this PARP inhibitor's AUC by 170%.",
